{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# GloVe, FastText, and Subword Embeddings Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### GloVe: factorize the co-occurrence matrix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_cooccurrence(docs, window=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pair_counts = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for doc in docs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token in doc:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if token not in vocab:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                vocab[token] = len(vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for doc in docs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indexed = [vocab[t] for t in doc]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, center in enumerate(indexed):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(max(0, i - window), min(len(indexed), i + window + 1)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if i != j:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    distance = abs(i - j)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    pair_counts[(center, indexed[j])] += 1.0 / distance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return vocab, pair_counts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def glove_train(vocab, pair_counts, dim=16, epochs=100, lr=0.05, x_max=100, alpha=0.75, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    W = rng.normal(0, 0.1, size=(n, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    W_tilde = rng.normal(0, 0.1, size=(n, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b_tilde = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for (i, j), x_ij in pair_counts.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            weight = (x_ij / x_max) ** alpha if x_ij < x_max else 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            diff = W[i] @ W_tilde[j] + b[i] + b_tilde[j] - np.log(x_ij)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            coef = weight * diff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grad_W_i = coef * W_tilde[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grad_W_tilde_j = coef * W[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            W[i] -= lr * grad_W_i"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            W_tilde[j] -= lr * grad_W_tilde_j"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            b[i] -= lr * coef"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            b_tilde[j] -= lr * coef"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return W + W_tilde"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two moving pieces worth naming. The weighting function `f(x) = (x/x_max)^alpha` downweights very frequent pairs (like `(the, and)`) so they do not dominate the loss. The final embedding is the sum of `W` (center) and `W_tilde` (context) tables. Summing both is a published trick that tends to outperform using just one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### FastText: subword-aware embeddings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def char_ngrams(word, n_min=3, n_max=6):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    wrapped = f\"<{word}>\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grams = {wrapped}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for n in range(n_min, n_max + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(wrapped) - n + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grams.add(wrapped[i:i + n])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return grams"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> char_ngrams(\"where\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{'<where>', '<wh', 'whe', 'her', 'ere', 're>', '<whe', 'wher', 'here', 'ere>', '<wher', 'where', 'here>'}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each word is represented by its set of n-grams (typically 3 to 6 characters). The word embedding is the sum of its n-gram embeddings. For skip-gram training, plug this in where Word2Vec used a single vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def fasttext_vector(word, ngram_table):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grams = char_ngrams(word)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vecs = [ngram_table[g] for g in grams if g in ngram_table]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not vecs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.sum(vecs, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For an unseen word, you still get a vector as long as some of its n-grams are known. `whereupon` shares `<wh`, `her`, `ere`, and `<where` with `where`, so the two land near each other."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### BPE: learned subword vocabulary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def learn_bpe(corpus, k_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for word, freq in corpus.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens = tuple(word) + (\"</w>\",)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vocab[tokens] = freq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    merges = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(k_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pair_freq = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for tokens, freq in vocab.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for a, b in zip(tokens, tokens[1:]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pair_freq[(a, b)] += freq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not pair_freq:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best = pair_freq.most_common(1)[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        merges.append(best)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        new_vocab = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for tokens, freq in vocab.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            new_tokens = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            i = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            while i < len(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if i + 1 < len(tokens) and (tokens[i], tokens[i + 1]) == best:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    new_tokens.append(tokens[i] + tokens[i + 1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    i += 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    new_tokens.append(tokens[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    i += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            new_vocab[tuple(new_tokens)] = freq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vocab = new_vocab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return merges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def apply_bpe(word, merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = list(word) + [\"</w>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for a, b in merges:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        new_tokens = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        i = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        while i < len(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if i + 1 < len(tokens) and tokens[i] == a and tokens[i + 1] == b:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                new_tokens.append(a + b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                i += 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                new_tokens.append(tokens[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                i += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens = new_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> corpus = Counter({\"low\": 5, \"lower\": 2, \"newest\": 6, \"widest\": 3})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> merges = learn_bpe(corpus, k_merges=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> apply_bpe(\"lowest\", merges)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "['low', 'est</w>']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "First iteration merges the most common adjacent pair. After enough iterations, frequent substrings (`low`, `est`, `tion`) become single tokens and rare words break cleanly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The real GPT / BERT / T5 tokenizers learn 30k-100k merges. Result: any text tokenizes into a bounded-length sequence of known IDs, no OOV ever."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `char_ngrams(\"playing\")` and `char_ngrams(\"played\")`. Compute the Jaccard overlap of the two n-gram sets. You should see substantial shared pieces (`pla`, `lay`, `play`), which is why FastText transfers well across morphological variants.\n2. **Medium.** Extend `learn_bpe` to track vocabulary growth. Plot tokens-per-corpus-character as a function of number of merges. You should see rapid compression at first, asymptoting near ~2-3 chars per token.\n3. **Hard.** Train a 1k-merge BPE on Shakespeare's complete works. Compare tokenization of common words vs. rare proper nouns. Measure average tokens per word before and after. Write up what surprised you."
      ]
    }
